        "raisedBy": [
          "accessibility"
        ],
        "recommendation": "Render the delete action as a native `<button type=\"button\" className=\"icon-button\" onClick={onDelete}>`. A keyboard user pressing Tab never lands on the div (no tabindex), and Enter or Space cannot trigger it (no key handler, no role), so the change's one feature — deleting a document — cannot be done without a mouse (WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard, 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value). The button gives focus, Enter/Space activation and the button role at once.",
